        "explanation": "Docker packages an application, its dependencies, Python runtime, and OS libraries into an immutable, portable Container Image.\n\nProduction Container Best Practices:\n1. Multi-Stage Builds:\n   The builder stage compiles wheels and installs build tools (gcc, make, headers). The slim final stage copies only the compiled wheels and virtualenv into a minimal distroless or alpine/slim runtime image, shrinking image sizes from 1.2GB down to ~90MB!\n2. Non-Root User:\n   Never run container processes as the default `root` user in production; create a dedicated unprivileged user (`appuser`).\n3. .dockerignore:\n   Exclude `.git`, `__pycache__`, `.venv`, `.env`, and test files from the build context to accelerate builds and avoid leaking secrets.\n4. docker-compose:\n   Coordinates multi-container setups (FastAPI app, PostgreSQL, Redis) with shared networks and persistent volumes.",
