        "topicNum": 48,
        "title": "Top Data Structures & Algorithms Patterns in Python (Two Pointers, Sliding Window, Heap)",
        "explanation": "Technical campus placement interviews at top product companies (Google, Amazon, Microsoft, TCS Digital) heavily emphasize algorithmic problem-solving.\n\nCore Algorithmic Patterns in Python:\n1. Two Pointers Pattern:\n   Used on sorted arrays/sequences. Two pointers iterate from opposite ends or at differing speeds (slow/fast pointers for cycle detection). Time complexity: O(n), Space: O(1).\n2. Sliding Window Pattern:\n   Maintains a dynamic window `[left, right]` over an array or string to find subarrays/substrings meeting specific criteria (e.g. longest substring without repeating characters). Reduces naive O(n^2) nested loops to linear O(n).\n3. Heap / Priority Queue (`heapq` module):\n   Min-heap by default. `heapq.heappush()` and `heapq.heappop()` operate in O(log k). Essential for Top-K Elements, Merging K-Sorted Lists, and Median Stream calculation.\n4. Binary Search (`bisect` module):\n   `bisect.bisect_left()` and `bisect.bisect_right()` locate insertion points in sorted arrays in O(log n) time.",
